<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap about-grid">
    <div class="about-photos reveal">
      <div class="about-tall"><img decoding="async" width="720" height="960" src="img/farnaz-carpet.webp" alt="Farnaz Sadeghian beside a large hand-knotted Persian carpet" data-i18n-alt="altCarpet" loading="lazy"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="aboutEyebrow">About Farnaz Sadeghian</p>
      <h2 data-i18n="aboutH2">A designer's eye, <em>made simple</em></h2>
      <p class="script" data-i18n="aboutQuote">“A beautiful home is not about spending more. It's about knowing what to choose.”</p>
      <p data-i18n="aboutP1">Farnaz has lived in Dubai for twelve years. She trained in interior decoration, earned her certification through TAFE in Australia, and spent the following years designing, consulting and staging real homes. More than fifty Dubai properties were staged by her, each one planned first in 3D.</p>
      <p data-i18n="aboutP2">That hands-on experience is what her followers learn from today. Every tip is something she has tested in a real room: how to place a sofa in a long living room, how to hide an awkward pillar, what to buy and what to skip.</p>
      <div class="facts">
        <div><b>50+</b><span data-i18n="fact1">homes staged with 3D design</span></div>
        <div><b data-i18n="fact2v">6 yrs</b><span data-i18n="fact2">professional practice</span></div>
        <div><b data-i18n="fact3v">TAFE</b><span data-i18n="fact3">certified interior decorator, Australia</span></div>
        <div><b data-i18n="fact4v">Mother of 3</b><span data-i18n="fact4">designing for real family life</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="journal" class="journal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="jr-head reveal">
      <div><p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="blogEyebrow">Style journal</p>
      <h2 data-i18n="blogH2">One interior style, <em>every day</em></h2></div>
      <p class="lead" data-i18n="blogLead">Short guides by Farnaz on a different home style each day: where it comes from, what defines it, and how to use it in a real home.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="jr-grid reveal">@@BLOGCARDS@@</div>
    <p class="jr-all"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="blog/"><span data-i18n="blogAll">All articles</span> <svg><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="transform">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ba-head reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="baEyebrow">Before &amp; after</p>
        <h2 data-i18n="baH2">Same room. <em>Different feeling.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lead" data-i18n="baLead">Most rooms don't need new walls. They need the right layout, light and a few well-chosen pieces. Drag the slider to see what styling changes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ba-tabs reveal" role="group">
      <button class="chip" type="button" data-scene="living" aria-pressed="true" data-i18n="baLiving">Living room</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" data-scene="bedroom" aria-pressed="false" data-i18n="baBedroom">Bedroom</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" data-scene="kitchen" aria-pressed="false" data-i18n="baKitchen">Kitchen</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" data-scene="dining" aria-pressed="false" data-i18n="baDining">Dining room</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" data-scene="entry" aria-pressed="false" data-i18n="baEntry">Entrance</button>
      <button class="chip" type="button" data-scene="kids" aria-pressed="false" data-i18n="baKids">Kids' room</button>
    </div>
    <div class="ba reveal" id="ba" dir="ltr" style="--pos:50%">
      <img decoding="async" width="1100" height="822" class="after" id="sceneAfter" src="img/ba-living-after.webp" alt="" data-i18n-alt="altBaA_living" loading="lazy">
      <img decoding="async" width="1100" height="824" class="before" id="sceneBefore" src="img/ba-living-before.webp" alt="" data-i18n-alt="altBaB_living" loading="lazy">
      <span class="lbl l" data-i18n="baBefore">Before</span><span class="lbl r" data-i18n="baAfter">After</span>
      <div class="handle-line"><div class="knob"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m9 6-6 6 6 6M15 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div></div>
      <label style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)" for="baRange" data-i18n="baAria">Compare before and after</label>
      <input type="range" id="baRange" min="0" max="100" value="50">
    </div>
    <p class="ba-note" data-i18n="baNote">Example rooms created to illustrate her method.</p>
    <h3 class="tips-h reveal" data-i18n="baTipsH">Four moves behind every <em>after</em></h3>
    <ol class="tips">
      <li class="tip reveal"><span class="tip-n">01</span><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"><rect x="5" y="14" width="30" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M5 22h30M11 14v16M29 14v16"/></svg><p data-i18n="step1">Anchor the seating with a rug sized to the room.</p></li>
      <li class="tip reveal"><span class="tip-n">02</span><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"><path d="M20 4v8M12 20a8 8 0 0 1 16 0z"/><path d="M17 24a3 3 0 0 0 6 0M10 34h20"/></svg><p data-i18n="step2">Layer light: a pendant, a floor lamp, warm bulbs.</p></li>
      <li class="tip reveal"><span class="tip-n">03</span><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"><rect x="8" y="8" width="24" height="20" rx="1"/><path d="m11 25 6-7 5 5 3-3 4 5"/><circle cx="25" cy="14" r="2"/></svg><p data-i18n="step3">Turn an empty wall into a focal point.</p></li>
      <li class="tip reveal"><span class="tip-n">04</span><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"><path d="M20 34V18M20 22c-6 0-9-4-9-10 6 0 9 4 9 10zM20 18c0-6 3-10 9-10 0 6-3 10-9 10z"/><path d="M13 34h14"/></svg><p data-i18n="step4">Soften with textiles and something living.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="learn">
